id: pm-rl-qix7
title: An approved generation budget the loop cannot advance past on its own
description: "A loop that promotes its own successors has no natural stopping point, and the useful stopping rule is not a compute limit but a human decision recorded where the loop can read it. pm-rl binds a self-improvement programme to an approval item that states how many generations are authorized and on what evidence. Advancing beyond that count is refused, and the refusal names the approval item that must be extended, so the operator is told exactly what to write rather than which flag to add. This is the same shape as the release approval already governing which packages may publish: the gate is a tracked decision, not an environment variable, so it survives a fresh checkout, is reviewable in a diff, and cannot be satisfied by a process that merely sets something."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T20:50:26.171Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T20:50:26.171Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: Advancing past the approved generation count exits non-zero and names the approval item to extend; extending the approval item permits exactly the additional generations it states; a programme with no approval item refuses at the first promotion rather than at the last; the budget is read from tracked project data and never from an environment variable
